    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "Harding-Turner Clinic\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI am writing to provide you with a comprehensive overview of Michael Russell's current medical condition following his consultation on February 04, 2025.\n\n**Medical History and Current Status:**\n\n**Pulmonary embolism / DVT:** Mr. Russell experienced a pulmonary embolism and deep vein thrombosis approximately four months ago, which has been well managed. Currently, he is on warfarin 7.5 mg, which has effectively controlled his condition. There have been no signs of recurrence or any complications related this condition.\n\n**Polycystic kidney Mr. Russell has been diagnosed with polycystic kidney disease since October 2006. His estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) is currently 43. Despite this, his condition remains stable and well-controlled. No specific medications are required for this condition at this time.\n\n**Urinary tract infection:** Mr. Russell has a history of urinary tract infections, with the most recent episode occurring in November 2011. He has been managing this condition with nitrofurantoin 100 mg, and it remains well-controlled. There have been no further episodes since his treatment.\n\n**Cataracts:** Mr. Russell has cataracts, which were diagnosed in July 2015. Currently, his cataracts are managed without the need for any medications.\n\n**Physical Examination:**\nOn examination, Mr. Russell was found to have a blood pressure of 124/75 mmHg and a weight of 173 pounds. His general physical examination revealed no abnormalities. Additionally, he reported occasional minor complaints such as occasional fatigue, which are considered typical for his age and current medical conditions.\n\n**Lifestyle and Social History:**\n\nMr. Russell is quite active, engaging in running exercises 3-4 times a week. His exercise routine is a vital component of his overall health management.\n\nSocially, Mr. Russell has a history of smoking cigarettes, having started in July 1974 and quitting September 2024. His smoking habit was approximately 1.5 packs per day, and he has been honest about his history. Currently, he consumes around four alcoholic drinks per week.\n\n**Impression and Recommendations:**\n\nBased on the current assessment, Mr. Russell's conditions are well-managed. His warfarin and nitrofurantoin dosages are appropriate, and there is no indication for any changes at this time. His polycystic kidney disease and cataracts are stable, with no immediate need for intervention.\n\nPlease feel free to contact me should you require any further information or have additional concerns regarding Mr. Russell's car"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "e.\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Margaret Riddle \nFamily Medicine Specialist \nHarding-Turner Clinic\n"
    }
